<title>RUSSIA: Stake of 33.3 pct in Russian Yukos to be auctioned.</title>
<headline>Stake of 33.3 pct in Russian Yukos to be auctioned.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 33.3 percent stake in Russian oil company Yukos, held in trust by Bank Menatep, is to be auctioned in an investment tender next month, a Federal Property Fund official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The starting price for the stake of 745.66 million shares will be $160 million and the winner will be obliged to invest $200 million in 1997-98, fund official Vladimir Yefimchik told Reuters.</p>
</text>
